## IDLE DECISION 2026-10-20 (3): SIDECHAIN LOW-CUT MATCHES THE PROTOTYPE (overrides earlier sections)

Attempt 1 stopped at RT-2. Nuke's shaper input and GR were +0.0564 to +0.0570 dB off at -12/-6/0 dBFS, against a 0.05 dB gate. The cause is the sidechain 100 Hz high-pass. Ours is the one-pole `y = x - lp` (pole exp(-2*pi*100/48000)), which is -0.0578 dB at 7 kHz. `dyn3.level_db` uses a first-order Butterworth (bilinear) high-pass at 100 Hz, which is -0.0008 dB there.

Fix: replace the sidechain high-pass with the same first-order Butterworth bilinear HPF at 100 Hz as `dyn3` (same coefficient formula and same state order), for every preset that has a sidechain HPF (check Natural and Glue as well as Nuke). Change it in Render (`bloom_dsp.py`) and Play (`bloom_live.inc`) together. Do not loosen the 0.05 dB RT-2 gate. Before running the full RT-2 set, pilot Nuke at 7 kHz, 0 dBFS, and require |dGR| < 0.005 dB. If the pilot fails, STOP and restore as before. Bloom off must stay bit-exact (the off path never touches this filter).

Restart Step 1 from Phase 0 (fresh preBLOOMRETRY backup check, DLL recipe straight to %LOCALAPPDATA%\Temp\live_stereo.dll), redo the colour-before-makeup edits, then add this fix before RT-2.
